{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-kou-21.48-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.48-0394123e-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T08:00:00Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-kou-21.48-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.48-0394123e-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-kou-21.48-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.48-0394123e-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-kou-21.48-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.48-0394123e-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/KOU-21.48"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "A quasimorphism on a group $G$ is a function $f:G\\to\\mathbb R$ such that the quantity $\\sup_{g,h}|f(g)+f(h)-f(gh)|$ is finite. A quasimorphism is homogeneous if it restricts to a homomorphism on every cyclic subgroup of $G$. Let $G$ be a group admitting an unbounded homogeneous quasimorphism $G\\to\\mathbb R$ that is not a homomorphism. Must $G$ contain a non-abelian free subgroup?"}, "statement_sha256": "35d2050a0ce029dc8b284dd21871d8bcdc83836f5da73109d42d762a7ae5f21f"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-kou-21.48-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.48-0394123e-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/KOU-21.48"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_